# In order to in Russian: чтобы
subtitle: "Open a bank account in Russian and learn что́бы: in order to with a to-form, and why \"I want you to come\" takes the past."
tags: ["russian","чтобы","in order to in russian","bank in russian","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/purpose-clauses","vocabulary/money-and-documents"]
thumb: "band \"In order to, in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"An eleventh Russian story: Tom's first week in Petersburg","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/110-russian-review-11.cast"}

